{
  "spec": "messaging section 3 + section 19 amendment A2; identity section 6.4 + section 14 - the sealed packet with a caller-owned inner (seal_payload/open_payload): known answers + negatives",
  "frozen": "2026-10-14",
  "description": "Same construction as sealed-packet.json (per-packet ephemeral X25519; shared = X25519(esk, rpk), abort on all-zero; key = BLAKE2b-256('111/seal/v1' || shared || epk || rpk); nonce = BLAKE2b-192('111/seal-n/v1' || epk || rpk); XChaCha20-Poly1305 with AD = the exact header bytes version || crypto_mode || counter(LE u64) || extra_len || extra; packet = header || epk || ciphertext||tag) EXCEPT that the AEAD plaintext is the caller's inner bytes verbatim - NO 32-byte sender NodeId (Layer 5 amendment A2: the sender is authenticated by Layer 5's pair_mac, which covers header || epk || inner, so seal_payload hands the closure the packet's epk and open_payload returns it). An empty inner is legal. 'kats' pin esk, so every intermediate is deterministic. 'negatives' are opened with open_payload under the recipient keyset; 'wrong_recipient' opens kats[0] under another keyset; 'seal_negatives' are refused by seal_payload before the inner closure runs. 'layout_ambiguity' freezes WHY two inner layouts may never share a version on a signed release: the wire cannot tell them apart. open_payload expect tokens: ok | err:truncated | err:mode:<m> | err:ecdh:<EcdhError> | err:auth (open_payload never yields err:short-plaintext). seal_negatives tokens: UnsupportedCryptoMode:<m> | HeaderTooLarge:<n> | Ecdh:<EcdhError>. u64 counters are decimal strings.",
  "provenance": "Generated 2026-10-14 (task L5-I1) from the spec text with crosscheck.py's from-scratch primitives (X25519 via OpenSSL, BLAKE2b via hashlib, HChaCha20 in pure Python + ChaCha20-Poly1305 via OpenSSL), no id111 code; esk values are published RFC 7748 section 5.2 material (the two scalar-multiplication inputs and the 1-iteration output). Asserted against the crate by seal.rs::payload_known_answer_vector (kats[0], hex pinned in-module) and tests/layer5_amendments.rs (every field, through the public seal_payload/open_payload and an in-test primitive-crate model), and re-derived by crosscheck.py (check_layer5_sealed).",
